    "title": "KoalaBear c2 (1,1,2) aligned positive ramified q-slice exclusion",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "all six aligned positive forced-ramified q-slice ideals are empty on the admissible open set",
    "statement": "Normalize J_0={2,1/2,b,1/b}, q(T)=T^2+tT+p, and the forced source branch to w=0. Exact positive reconstruction has two internal templates and three residual UFD allocations. Its relative scales are 3(2b-1)(p-1)(p+2t+4) in fixed-moving and -3(b^2-1)(p-1)(p+2t+4)(5p+4t+5) in moving-moving. After retaining that scale, removing only proved nonzero factors, and saturating by every endpoint, orbit, discriminant, normalization, and reconstruction factor, all three fixed-moving ideals are unit over F_2130706433. The moving equations are reciprocal quartics in b; exact descent to s=b+1/b makes all three corresponding saturated ideals unit. Thus no aligned positive forced-ramified candidate passes the necessary q-slice identity. Combined with the aligned-negative theorem, the complete aligned w=0 branch is empty; aligned positive w!=0 and the near-aligned homogeneous endpoint boundary remain open.",
